<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2572" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anguĭnĕus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		anguis, less freq. than the foll. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>pertaining to the
			serpent</i>, <i>snaky</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gorgonis comae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 4, 7, 12</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Similar to a serpent in form</i>, <i>serpent-like</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cucumis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 9, 10</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">7, 10,
		5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
